WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.240
Oh, my God.

00:00:01.245 --> 00:00:02.180
Oh, my God.

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.300
A woman records what appears to be a live

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.640
cow being pushed by a bulldozer.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:07.560
On that bulldozer?

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.430
Yes. He's alive.

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:11.220
She was filming from public land.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.930
The farm owner drove up and confronted her.

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:17.740
You cannot videotape my property from public property

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.360
Why are you concerned about being filmed

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:21.560
if you have no problem,

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.300
you think this is a legitimate business?

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.900
It is a legitimate business.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.900
Utah prosecutors charged the woman with

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.720
“agricultural operation interference.”

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:31.420
Am I free to leave or am I being detained?

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.380
You’re being detained.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.080
But she was on public land.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.820
They dropped the charges several months later.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:37.900
[Cow mooing]

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:40.340
But what if she’d sneaked on to a farm

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.580
to record what she considered animal abuse?

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.380
More than a hundred such investigations

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:46.040
have been done.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.280
Activists pose as farm workers

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:51.500
and secretly record the way animals are treated.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.940
An animal rights group released this

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.260
undercover video of the dairy farm.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.260
It shows workers hitting,

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:59.400
kicking, and throwing young calves.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.476
We are not showing the most disturbing parts

00:01:01.476 --> 00:01:02.090
of the video.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:04.439
Farmers, upset up about these recordings,

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:06.360
are persuading politicians to

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.840
essentially outlaw these undercover investigations.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.760
The controversial Ag-Gag law

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.479
the sixth state to pass an Ag-Gag law.

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:18.280
There are activists stalking farms to try to capture

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:21.380
something that the public doesn't understand.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.649
Kay Johnson Smith speaks for a farm group

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:26.060
that supports the ag-gag laws,

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.039
though they don’t call them that.

00:01:28.039 --> 00:01:30.780
We would call it farm protection. Farm protection.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.220
What about everybody else?

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.180
Why do you get special protection?

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:36.980
The agricultural community is the only business

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:39.140
community that this sort of tactic

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:41.670
is really being used on right now.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.100
I'm an investigative reporter,

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.880
I can't do my job if there are laws

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:48.200
that prevent me from showing things.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.040
Nobody believes it if you don't see it.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:53.700
These activist groups want

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:56.060
to eliminate all of animal agriculture.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:57.880
Brittany you’re holding a dead body

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:00.780
This group livestreams its protests on Facebook.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.390
You saw a dumpster with hundreds of dead birds?

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.360
Many of the activists stormed into the farm.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:08.149
Some stole some of the baby ducklings.

00:02:08.149 --> 00:02:12.580
We were just able to rescue almost 30 baby ducks.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.640
Others chained themselves to the entrance of the farm

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:17.160
[Music]

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.420
Later the activists released this video of

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:22.100
the 30 stolen ducklings, adding music,

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:25.620
and showing the birds running around, apparently happy

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:26.700
[Music]

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.900
They stole these ducks after seeing this earlier

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:32.540
undercover video of injured ducks at the farm.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:35.620
Mercy for Animals says their undercover investigations

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:37.049
have led to criminal charges.

00:02:37.049 --> 00:02:39.840
Ag-gag laws often prevent such investigations--

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.400
which is why farm states pass them.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.220
A bill making it illegal to apply for a job

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:48.140
in a farming operation under false pretenses.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:49.780
But what about free speech?

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:52.480
Ag-gag laws chill speech.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.360
Lawyer Amanda Howell speaks for the

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.020
Animal Legal Defense Fund, a group that says

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:59.280
ag-gag laws are unconstitutional.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.230
And they did get several states’ laws struck down.

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:05.340
Iowa, then, just passed a new law.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.110
Ag-Gag 2.0.

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:10.140
A bipartisan bill trying again to stop people

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.959
from lying to get onto farms.

00:03:11.959 --> 00:03:14.819
These groups are exposing issues that are happening.

00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:16.480
If they really cared about animals,

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:18.180
they would stop it right then.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:22.200
Instead, they go weeks and months without reporting

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.519
anything to the farm owners.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:27.100
That’s true. This investigation went on for months.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:30.080
Agriculture groups now are pushing laws that would

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:34.430
force activists to report abuse quickly. Why don’t they?

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:35.900
They want to make their movie.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.379
They want to make their sensational video.

00:03:38.379 --> 00:03:39.780
It's because they care about the animals

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.880
that they want to show that that's something that

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:43.520
happens every day on these farms

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:45.540
Consistent, constant, abuse

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:47.880
A company can say, "This is a one-off."

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:51.060
This is not just discrete actors. This is company policy.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:52.720
They say they don't want to just correct

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:54.260
the abuse on that farm.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:57.740
They want to change all farming practices.

00:03:57.740 --> 00:03:59.980
What they really want is to stop people from

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:01.120
eating meat, milk, and eggs.

00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:02.960
Do you want people to stop eating meat?

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:07.860
I want people to act in their conscience.

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:09.900
But you didn't really the question.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:16.660
Do you want people to stop eating meat or eggs?

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:22.500
I think that… again … I… I...

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:23.660
[laughs]

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:26.400
Are we asking... sorry... Are we asking me personally or

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.600
asking the Animal Legal Defense Fund?

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:30.919
She never did give a direct answer

00:04:30.919 --> 00:04:33.340
Workers in a turkey farm abusing the birds

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:35.900
Animal rights activists have exposed things

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.300
that need exposing.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:40.000
Wal-Mart now taking a stand when it comes

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.820
to the treatment of farm raised animals.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:44.600
How else would you have made these changes

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:46.940
without sneaking into your farms?

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:49.470
Well, that's to say that farmers can't be

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.800
trusted and I think that everyone-

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.990
And in the past, some could not.

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:56.680
There are bad apples in every industry.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:00.760
However, I would say 99.9% of farmers in America

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:02.780
They do the right thing every single day.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.760
Farming isn’t always pretty.

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:09.380
[Farm sounds]

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:11.740
People have some right to privacy, no?

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:14.500
I think we should all be worried when corporations

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.240
are supporting laws that impinge our right

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:17.106
to free speech.

00:05:17.106 --> 00:05:18.380
We should worry,

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.100
whatever you think of the activists,

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.160
and I have problems with many of them,

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.600
government shouldn’t pass special laws

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:27.780
that prevent people from revealing what’s true.

